The first round has $72$ matches. The second round has $36$ matches, the third round has $18$ matches, and so on. The total number of matches is
\begin{align*} 72+36+18+6+2 &= 134 \\ &= 2\cdot67 \\ \end{align*}
The answer is $\boxed{\textbf{(B)}}$.

Let $x$ be the time she drove in the sun and $y$ be the time she drove in the rain. We have the following system of equations:
\begin{align*} 30x+20y&=16, \\ x+y&=40/60=2/3. \end{align*}
Solving the second equation for $x$, we get $x=2/3-y$. Substituting this into the first equation, we get $30(2/3-y)+20y=16$, which simplifies to $20y=16-20/3=8/3$. Solving for $y$, we get $y=8/3\cdot 1/20=1/15$. Converting this to minutes, we get $y=1/15\cdot 60=\boxed{\textbf{(A)}\ 4}$ minutes.
